error: `fill` on the reader of a connection holds the thread until it is done, and an async function does not hold its thread
  the tasks of async functions share a few threads: one that holds its thread keeps the others from running
  --> error_net_reader_fill_blocking.sg:4:20
 4 |     _ = try reader.fill()
   |                    ^^^^
  hint: `await reader.fillAsync()` does the same work without holding the thread
